 we're like well  it's not as if he doesn't know what he's  doing  clearly he understands exactly what  what's happening here  and what he's doing then he finishes  like the next you know three minutes of  his paper  and that's it and then you know we go on  to the next thing  nobody said anything because i think  nobody  including myself had any idea of what it  was that we should say  should we confront this guy and say you  were really kind of a jerk  and what's the deal you're the person  who's supposed to be preventing  jerkiness so what what was going on  there  you know and none of us actually really  knew him  so we knew him by reputation but none of  us knew him personally so we didn't  we didn't want to ask like was that joe  that you were talking to  or michael or you know your wife or  or what he never said a word about it  and you know a few of us afterwards as  we're walking away we're talking with  ourselves we're  between ourselves and we're like what  did what were you what were your  reactions to that  and there's oh i could see that you were  trying not to laugh  and why were we trying not to laugh well  because what he was doing was so clearly  out of place and he was the person who  was supposed to be preventing that but  instead he was doing it  and so it was kind of comedic on the one  hand like watching somebody who just  doesn't have any class  and yet he's coming from this place  where they're all sort of  you know at least by reputation poshy  posh people you know the upper class  and uh supposed to be you know  representing an illustrious institution  not like the rest of us schlubs coming  from  wherever right and so it was so  incongruous that we we didn't really  know  what to make of it and when we were  comparing notes later  afterwards talking over a beer everyone  had had the same reaction they were like  well i thought maybe you would say  something no i thought you would say  something  and then everyone was like i was trying  just not to start laughing because i  didn't want to  you know if there was something like  actually wrong with him i didn't want to  hurt his feelings on the other hand he  was being kind of a jerk  and i don't think i should be like you  know laughing about him  being a jerk and so none of us knew what  to do  i mean i think if i'm in a situation  like that again i probably would react  differently  but none of us at the time had any idea  about  what was going on or what we should do  and and  so i'm not going to say that you know we  should like view this as a  you know humanity writ large moment or  anything like that but  you know i don't even know the guy's  name anymore it's so long ago but if i  ever ran into him i probably would ask  him about it  and i certainly would judge him for the  behavior that he displayed at that time  but who knows it could have been just  like the one day that he  behaved in a crazy foolish  manner or maybe he's like that all the  time  it's going to be kind of a mystery  you

